# ReadFlow

Turn any PDF into something you can listen to.

PDFs stay in the browser. Speech uses a voice on this device unless you configure a studio provider below.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).

## Speech providers

Device voices work with no configuration. To use a studio voice, set one of these in `.env.local` and restart the server:

```bash
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=tts-1-hd

ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_multilingual_v2

GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY=

AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=eastus

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
```

The first configured provider becomes the automatic voice. You can switch voices in Reading settings.
